<title>USA: BFGoodrich sees 1996 EPS of $2.81.</title>
<headline>BFGoodrich sees 1996 EPS of $2.81.</headline>
<dateline>RICHFIELD, Ohio 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>BFGoodrich Co said it expects to report 1996 earnings of about $2.81 a share, an increase from $2.15 a share in 1995, and expects a &quot;significant increase&quot; in 1997.</p>
<p>Excluding special items in both years, the company expects earnings in 1996 of about $2.22 a share, compared with $1.90 a share in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;We achieved the earnings target that we set for our company for the year and expect a significant increase once again in 1997,&quot; said BFGoodrich Chief Executive David Burner.</p>
<p>BFGoodrich, which provides aircraft systems and services and manufactures specialty chemicals, plans to announce its fourth quarter and full year results on February 18.</p>
<p>(( New York newsdesk 212-859-1610 ))</p>
